  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Plants have chlorophyll a, which is the primary pigment for the light reaction, but they also have other pigments called accessory pigments.
(a) What are the accessory pigments? (1.5 marks)
(b) What are the roles of accessory pigments in photosynthesis? (1.5 marks)', '(a) Accessory pigments are the light-absorbing pigments other than chlorophyll a: chlorophyll b, the carotenoids (carotenes such as β-carotene, and xanthophylls) and, in some algae and cyanobacteria, phycobilins (phycoerythrin, phycocyanin). (b) They absorb light of wavelengths that chlorophyll a absorbs poorly (e.g. blue-green and green) and transfer the absorbed energy to chlorophyll a in the reaction centre, so a wider range of light is used for photosynthesis; carotenoids also protect chlorophyll and the photosystems from photo-oxidation by excess light.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Pigments other than chlorophyll a: chlorophyll b, carotenoids (carotenes, xanthophylls), phycobilins (in algae)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "(b) Absorb light of other wavelengths and pass the energy to chlorophyll a (wider range of light used); protect chlorophyll from photo-oxidation", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'bio-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
